course: dictionary
lesson: 1260
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Burp can be a verb (an action) or a noun (a thing you can have). In «Kieran competes with Sam at everything: ... who can burp the alphabet furthest», burp is something you do, so it is a verb.
explain: «Cows burp methane, a strong warming gas» tells us the burp is the gas coming up and out. The word burp is the action here. In a sentence like «The fizzy drink left a loud burp», the word is a noun, a name for the noise itself.
explain: Context also tells you about the feeling or the setting. Burping in front of other people is not rude when you say excuse me and cover your mouth. Burp a baby is a special phrase. It means to pat a baby's back so it can bring up air after feeding.
fact: To burp means to let air come up from your stomach out through your mouth with a noise.
fact: A burp is that noise. You can let out a burp.
fact: To burp a baby means to pat its back to help it bring up air after feeding.
fact: Fizzy drinks cause burps because of the gas in them.
fact: After a burp, cover your mouth and say excuse me.
exercise: «Kieran can burp the alphabet furthest.» What does burp mean here? | To drink a fizzy drink quickly | To pat a baby's back | *To let air come up from your stomach with a noise | To sing loudly
exercise: A parent says, «Please burp the baby after her feed.» What does burp mean here? | To put her to sleep in her cot | To pat her back to help her bring up air | To give her a bottle of milk | *To pat her back to help her bring up air after feeding
exercise: «The fizzy drink left a loud burp in the room.» In this sentence, burp is a | verb, an action with no noise | name for a drink | name for a cow | *noun, a name for the noise
test: «Cows burp methane, a strong warming gas.» What does this tell us? | *Cows let methane come up from their stomachs | Cows make milk with methane | Cows eat fizzy drinks | Cows sleep in the sun all day
test: After a burp in a classroom, what is the polite thing to say? | Laugh loudly and ask for more | Say nothing and walk off | *Excuse me | Shout the alphabet
exam: Which sentence uses burp as a noun? | Kieran will burp the alphabet. | *A loud burp rang out from the back row. | The cow will burp soon. | Please burp the baby now.
